 "about_text": "Nonaka-Hill is a contemporary art gallery in Los Angeles founded in 2018 by Rodney and Taka Nonaka-Hill, with a second space in Kyoto, Japan. The program centers on modern and contemporary Japanese art, presenting many artists for the first time on the West Coast, spanning painting, ceramics, sculpture, and photography from postwar and contemporary Japan alongside a smaller group of international artists. Located in Hollywood near the intersection of Melrose and Highland, the gallery sits among a cluster of established Los Angeles galleries. Nonaka-Hill represents the estate of Yōga painter Zenzaburo Kojima and has built a program bridging Japanese art history with contemporary practice, participating regularly in international art fairs including Frieze, Art Basel, and Art Collaboration Kyoto.",
